<title>USA: Norwich Financial completes branch buys.</title>
<headline>Norwich Financial completes branch buys.</headline>
<dateline>NORWICH, Conn. 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwich Financial Corp said its Norwich Savings Society subsidiary completed its acquisition of two branches of First Union Bank of Connecticut.</p>
<p>Under terms of the agreement, announced last October, the First Union branches were merged with the bank's existing offices in New London and Groton.</p>
<p>The acquisition included the transfer of about $25 million in deposits and $1 million in loans, the company said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212e-859-1610))</p>
